Z||000021||sqoach||04-19-2001||06:25 PM||||Air is definately not a problem. The fan works fine and I never just sit there and idle.<P>I have a question for anyone. Is it possible to have too much coolant in the system? (not including the overflow bottle)||||reg||1
Z||000022||DJRice||04-19-2001||09:09 PM||||What engine do you have?<P>Have you done any work to the engine?  Was it rebuilt or anything like that?<P>Do you remember any significant event between when the car ran normally and its current condition?<P>When you turn on the AC, does the cooling fan turn on?<P>When you ground the green/white wire going to temp sending switch, does the cooling fan turn on?<P>Have you checked your coolant tubes that run from the front to the back of the car to see if they are bent or damaged in any way?<P>Other comments....<P>Rodded Radiator does not necessarily mean a good radiator.  The Fiero's cooling system is a bit unique in that the coolant does alot of travelling around.  Is a new radiator completely out of the question?<P>If you have a V6, you should definitely consider pulling the water pump and inspecting your impeller.  At this point I would have pulled all the hoses and ran water through all the hoses, tubes, radiator, and the engine to make sure things were flowing normally.  <P>I know you feel like you have checked everything, but your problem has been going on so long you should start from scratch <B><I>one more time</B></I> and double check the proper operation of <B><I>every component</B></I> in the system.  I know you feel like you have done everything, but you cant have done it all because the thing still does not work.  <P>Take a step back and approach the problem as if it were the first time you have experienced it.  Your problem is that you are so frustrated, you may be missing something obvious.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<p>[This message has been edited by DJRice (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||strdream||04-19-2001||09:42 PM||||I am still going to stay with the head gasket. It is possible that the only symptom at first is air in the coolant. When the fire ring of the gasket deteriorates the extreem pressure of combustion penitrates the gasket.  The gasket my still be well able to hold coolant and oil in but not hold the cobustion pressure. Each time it fires a tiny bubble sqeaks thru. in time you have an air lock and over heat.  As it gets worse it will show more symptoms.<P>You can test it yourself if you remove the T-stat, make sure it is full of coolant. With a closed system let it run at a high idle 1500-2000 RPMs and watch the over flow bottle. You may have to look down inside for air bubbles.  buy the time it is warmed up you will see air bubbles coming into the bottle. If it is not leaking bad you may see a bubble every 5 -15 sec. if it is bad you will see a steady stream. any leak is not tolerable.<BR>Ross ||||reg||1
Z||000024||sqoach||04-20-2001||12:01 PM||||DJRice, it's a 2.5L 5spd with A/C.<BR>I really don't think the engine has ever been rebuilt. I had to change the valve cover gasket a while back and you could tell it was very old. Probably the stock one. And of course this made me think that other gaskets would be bad, but I didn't mess with it and I didn't have the money or time to do a complete rebuild.<BR>The very first time I had my car overheat was because the fan went out. I was doing a lot of city driving and when I stopped one time, noticed some coolant under my car. After that I can't remember too well. But now my fan works, and the fan switch works. And getting a new radiator now is not likely at all. I'm about broke.<BR>I've checked the hoses and pipes many times. The other day I had my car raised up and went under it checking for anything. All looks ok. There are no external leaks anywhere.<P>strdream, that sounds possible. I've been thinking that somewhere, just a little bit of air has been getting in each time I run my car. My dad doesn't think it's the head gasket because my oil and my coolant look normal still.<BR>And I'll try that test today probably.<P>Thanks guys.||||reg||1
